# Secrets & local env
# Ignore ALL .env variants (incl. .bak copies) except the safe template.
# A narrow `.env` + `.env.*.local` once let .env.bak-180754 slip in with real creds.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# 02_selectors_repo — ALLOWLIST, not a blacklist. Everything in this folder is
# ignored by default, whatever it is called; only the files re-included below are
# committed. This is deliberate: raw Playwright codegen captures the LOGIN steps
# verbatim (typed username + password), and a codegen export can land under any
# name/format (codegen.ts, a .har, a .json, "new 2.txt") — a blacklist would let a
# credential-bearing file sail straight through.
#
# Recordings (*recording*.txt) ARE committed — they are the codegen source that
# `import-codegen` consumes, so keeping them reviewable in git is worth it. The
# catch: they must be credential-SCRUBBED first (login value replaced with the
# <<USERNAME>> / <<PASSWORD>> placeholder — the literal is never used because login
# runs through the shared flows/login.csv reusable). This is ENFORCED by the
# pre-commit guard scripts/check-recordings.ts (npm run check-recordings), which
# blocks any commit whose recordings still hold a real credential. Do NOT allowlist
# other codegen formats here (.ts/.har/.json) — they are not guard-checked.
**/02_selectors_repo/**
!**/02_selectors_repo/selectors.csv
!**/02_selectors_repo/locators.json
!**/02_selectors_repo/*[Rr]ecording*.txt

# Node
node_modules/

# Run outputs (never committed)
artifacts/
reports/
**/07_actual_results/*.csv
**/08_diffs/*
**/09_html_report/*

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/
.auth/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# NOTE: 06_baseline/ is intentionally NOT ignored — baselines are committed.
# Generated POM/spec files ARE committed so diffs are reviewable, but are never hand-edited.

# Local-only AI/session context (handoff notes) — NEVER commit these.
*.local.md
